title: Capital letters do not carry stress.
pid: 9dbd6fb7-99b8-428e-8eab-bc9aab97d68f
body: |2-
    In comments, docstrings, docs and user-visible messages, write a word
    in lowercase unless it is an acronym or a proper name in letters
    (HEAD, UUID, TOML, ID, SKG), a placeholder in a wire grammar (GITREPO,
    PATH), a label that heads a comment section ('PURPOSE:', 'PITFALL:',
    'NOTE:'), an org keyword, or a word whose sentence warns of something
    whose neglect breaks the program or the data. Where caps would carry
    a sentence's stress, reword the sentence to carry it.
